      "id": "claim_0516a09a43da4c51b656955ff8eef6f3",
      "statement": "Nearly all /api prefixes mount requireAuth; the exceptions are /auth (empty middleware, public login), /swarms/spawns (requireAuthOrSpawnToken admits either a user JWT or scoped X-Spawn-Token, while POST /spawns/root still requires write:swarm_action so token-only children cannot create roots), /swarm-v2/social-runtime, /api/health, /telegram (secret webhook), and the public GET /api/version direct route.",
